NOTE: Follow this rule when creating or editing GitHub issues via `gh issue create` / `gh issue edit`, drafting briefs under `docs/issues/`, or implementing **features** / **fixes** under `modules/` and `bin/`.

## Title notation

```
{semantic}/PPT-{NNN}: [{domain}] {Title in sentence case}
```

| Part | Values | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| `semantic` | Prefer Conventional Commit types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore` (+ repo extras `ops`, `ci` when apt) | `feat/PPT-034` |
| `PPT-{NNN}` | Next program ID; label must match (`PPT-032`) | `PPT-041` |
| `domain` | `[api]`, `[model]`, `[EPIC][api]` for epics only | `[model]` |
| Epic | Prefix domain with `[EPIC]` | `feat/PPT-032: [EPIC][api] …` |

**Do not** use `PPT-0##: semantic(api):` — semantic comes **before** the program ID.

Issue/PR/commit type should track [Semantic Commit Messages](https://gist.github.com/joshbuchea/6f47e86d2510bce28f8e7f42ae84c716) / Conventional Commits. Map work as follows:

| Work | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|--------|
| New user-facing capability | `feat` | — |
| Bug fix **or** security/posture hardening that changes production behavior | `fix` | `harden`, `perf` (unless truly performance-only) |
| Docs-only | `docs` | — |
| Tests-only | `test` | — |
| No production code (tooling grunt) | `chore` | using `chore` for real API/security code changes |
| Infra/runbooks/CI wiring | `ops` or `ci` (repo extras) | inventing new verbs |

```text
✅ feat/PPT-036: [api] Accounts and categories CRUD (v3 model)
✅ fix/PPT-044: [api] Post-MVP API security and operational hardening
✅ ops/PPT-045: [api] Standardize uvicorn packaging in Compose
✅ feat/PPT-032: [EPIC][api] FastAPI MVP on v3 model + Supabase PostgreSQL
❌ harden/PPT-044: [api] …          ← not an official commit type
❌ PPT-039: ops(api): Supabase B1…  ← wrong ordering
❌ feat(api): FastAPI MVP             ← missing PPT-NNN
```

## Labels

Apply the matching `PPT-{NNN}` label plus domain labels (`API`, `data model`, `CI/CD`, `documentation`, etc.).

## Code paths (feat / fix / docs / test / ops)

| Semantic | Domain | Primary paths |
|----------|--------|---------------|
| `feat`, `fix` | `[model]` | `modules/model/src/`, `modules/model/tests/`, `modules/model/alembic/` |
| `feat`, `fix` | `[api]` | `modules/api/src/`, `modules/api/tests/` |
| `ops`, `fix`, `ci` | `[infra]` | `bin/`, `docker/`, `.github/`, `Makefile` |
| `test` | any | `modules/**/tests/`, `.github/workflows/` |

When closing code for a feature or fix, the PR/issue body should cite the touched paths under **Tasks / deliverables** or **References**.

